WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.064
A recipe is a JSON file that sets up an Orchard Core site.

00:00:05.064 --> 00:00:10.334
It enables features, changes settings, and creates content types and content.

00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:15.350
In this video, you write one for a module, give it variables, and run it.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:23.547
A recipe is a file whose name ends in .recipe.json.

00:00:23.547 --> 00:00:27.775
Put it directly in the Recipes folder of a module or a theme,

00:00:27.775 --> 00:00:30.173
and Orchard Core finds it there.

00:00:30.173 --> 00:00:35.410
The module project embeds the file, so it needs no entry in the project file.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.678
The file holds three kinds of content:

00:00:38.678 --> 00:00:42.913
properties that describe the recipe, variables, and a list of steps.

00:00:42.913 --> 00:00:46.748
Orchard Core runs the steps from the first to the last, and a

00:00:46.748 --> 00:00:48.980
step that fails stops the recipe.

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:52.180
Each step is an object with a name.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:56.542
The name picks the step, and the other properties are its settings.

00:00:56.542 --> 00:01:02.040
A step whose name no handler recognizes is skipped, so a misspelled name does nothing.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:08.829
The first properties describe the recipe.

00:01:08.829 --> 00:01:12.794
The name identifies it, and other recipes use that name to run it.

00:01:12.794 --> 00:01:16.870
The displayName and the description are what the Recipes page lists.

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:21.805
Tags appear as badges next to the recipe, and the Recipes page leaves

00:01:21.805 --> 00:01:23.646
out a recipe tagged hidden.

00:01:23.646 --> 00:01:28.110
The author, the website, and the version are information about the recipe.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:33.601
A recipe that sets issetuprecipe to true is offered on the setup screen,

00:01:33.601 --> 00:01:36.094
and the Recipes page leaves it out.

00:01:36.094 --> 00:01:41.200
Leave the property out of a recipe that you run on a site that already exists.

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:43.774
The file is read leniently:

00:01:43.774 --> 00:01:46.371
comments and trailing commas are allowed.

00:01:46.371 --> 00:01:49.410
Use a comment to explain a step where it appears.

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:56.567
A script is a string in square brackets:

00:01:56.567 --> 00:01:59.010
a prefix, a colon, and the code.

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:03.510
The prefix js runs JavaScript, and the prefix file reads a file.

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:08.010
Any other prefix is not evaluated, and its brackets are removed.

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:12.696
Variables hold values that you define once and use in any step.

00:02:12.696 --> 00:02:17.087
Declare them in the variables object, before the steps, and read one in

00:02:17.087 --> 00:02:19.540
a script with the variables function.

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:25.845
Orchard Core evaluates a variable the first time a step reads it, and keeps the result.

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:30.444
A variable that calls uuid gives one identifier to the whole recipe, so

00:02:30.444 --> 00:02:33.490
two steps can point at the same content item.

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:36.855
Scripts can read their surroundings too.

00:02:36.855 --> 00:02:41.516
The configuration function reads a tenant configuration key, with a default.

00:02:41.516 --> 00:02:45.950
The parameters function reads values such as AdminUsername and SiteName.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:50.529
To keep long text out of the recipe, put it in a file beside it.

00:02:50.529 --> 00:02:54.413
A step reads the file with the file prefix and the text function,

00:02:54.413 --> 00:02:57.641
and the path is relative to the folder of the recipe.

00:02:57.641 --> 00:02:59.610
A variable cannot read a file.

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:05.859
Start with the feature step.

00:03:05.859 --> 00:03:10.741
Its enable property lists the features to turn on, and its disable property

00:03:10.741 --> 00:03:12.972
lists the features to turn off.

00:03:12.972 --> 00:03:17.492
In a recipe run from Tools, Recipes, or during setup, the steps after

00:03:17.492 --> 00:03:19.240
it use what it enables.

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:23.420
A theme is a feature too, so enable it before you set it.

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:27.122
The themes step sets the site theme and the admin theme, and a

00:03:27.122 --> 00:03:30.770
property that is missing or empty leaves that theme as it is.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:36.864
The settings step changes site settings, such as SiteName, TimeZoneId, and HomeRoute.

00:03:36.864 --> 00:03:40.915
Any other property is stored under its own name, which is how a

00:03:40.915 --> 00:03:44.380
feature's settings, like the layer settings, are set.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:52.705
The ContentDefinition step creates content types and parts.

00:03:52.705 --> 00:03:55.498
The BakeryPage type lists three parts:

00:03:55.498 --> 00:03:58.862
TitlePart, HtmlBodyPart, and a part of its own.

00:03:58.862 --> 00:04:02.860
PartName is the part, and Name is what the type calls it.

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:05.536
A part lists its fields.

00:04:05.536 --> 00:04:10.801
The BakeryPage part has one field, a text field named OpeningHours, with the

00:04:10.801 --> 00:04:12.920
display name Opening Hours.

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:17.142
If a type or part already exists, the step alters it.

00:04:17.142 --> 00:04:21.321
It adds the parts and fields you list, and merges their settings.

00:04:21.321 --> 00:04:25.500
A type's own settings merge only when the type has a DisplayName.

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:30.234
The content step creates content items from its data array.

00:04:30.234 --> 00:04:36.241
Each item names its ContentType, has a ContentItemId, and sets Latest and Published to true.

00:04:36.241 --> 00:04:41.390
Take the ContentItemId from a variable, and other steps can point at the item.

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:45.300
Each part's data sits under the part's name.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:50.608
TitlePart holds a Title, HtmlBodyPart holds Html, and a text field holds Text.

00:04:50.608 --> 00:04:54.210
Owner and Author come from the parameters function.

00:04:58.420 --> 00:05:03.469
Tools, Recipes lists the recipes of the modules and themes, grouped by module.

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:05.272
Let's search for Bakery.

00:05:05.272 --> 00:05:10.320
The Bakery Starter module holds our recipe, with its description and its tags.

00:05:10.772 --> 00:05:13.168
Select Run, and confirm with Yes.

00:05:13.168 --> 00:05:18.452
Orchard Core runs the steps in order, from the feature step to the content step.

00:05:18.915 --> 00:05:23.827
A notification reports that the recipe Bakery Pages has been run successfully.

00:05:23.827 --> 00:05:28.446
When a step fails, the notification names the recipe and lists the errors

00:05:28.446 --> 00:05:30.025
of that step instead.

00:05:30.477 --> 00:05:34.220
The home page of the site shows the Bakery Page that the recipe

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:38.397
created, with its title, its text from the file, and the opening hours.

00:05:42.597 --> 00:05:47.517
Other features add their own steps, such as Roles, Templates, and Layers.

00:05:47.517 --> 00:05:52.437
The documentation shows many of the built-in steps, each with an example.

00:05:53.187 --> 00:05:58.013
The ReloadTenant step asks the tenant to reload, so that settings read only

00:05:58.013 --> 00:06:01.170
at startup, such as CORS policies, take effect.

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:04.567
Place it after the steps that write those settings.

00:06:05.317 --> 00:06:08.185
The recipes step runs other recipes by name.

00:06:08.185 --> 00:06:12.544
Each named recipe runs right after that step, before the next one, and

00:06:12.544 --> 00:06:15.757
a name that no recipe has is reported as an error.

00:06:16.507 --> 00:06:19.306
A data migration can run a recipe as well.

00:06:19.306 --> 00:06:24.322
Inject the IRecipeMigrator, and call ExecuteAsync with the file name of a recipe

00:06:24.322 --> 00:06:27.238
kept in the Migrations folder of the module.

00:06:27.238 --> 00:06:31.437
Register the migration with AddDataMigration in the Startup class.

00:06:32.187 --> 00:06:35.981
A data migration runs while the tenant is being activated.

00:06:35.981 --> 00:06:40.487
When a migration runs a recipe, the content step waits and imports its

00:06:40.487 --> 00:06:43.333
items after all migrations have completed.

00:06:43.333 --> 00:06:48.077
In a recipe that you run from Tools, Recipes, it imports them immediately.

00:06:50.077 --> 00:06:51.487
That is a recipe:

00:06:51.487 --> 00:06:57.742
properties, variables, and steps that enable features, define content types, and create content,

00:06:57.742 --> 00:07:02.402
written in the Recipes folder of a module and run from Tools, Recipes.

00:07:02.402 --> 00:07:03.997
Thanks for watching.

